{
  "why": "The touch session law every viewport host obeys: raw contacts with a clock in, host steps out (the primary press is deferred until the finger has decided, a held finger is an additive press that asks for its long press at the deadline while it is still down, a decided tap says `tap`, two fingers are the camera). `deadlines` (when present) is the wake time `nextDeadlineMs` after each event, `null` when nothing waits on the clock. `orbit` rows pin the pinch-to-orbit law against the TypeScript `applyPinchToOrbit` (values produced by that function). Language-agnostic: a TypeScript or other twin replays the same rows.",
